 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## On-device translation
+
+The header has a **Translate** control (the language icon next to the reading list). It translates article headlines, summaries, captions, body text and teasers right in the browser, using Chrome's built-in [Translator](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/translator-api) and [Language Detector](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/language-detection) APIs. No article text is sent to a server.
+
+- To make an element translatable, add the `data-translatable` attribute. To exclude something inside it, add `translate="no"` or `data-no-translate`.
+- Each region's source language is detected on the device, falling back to the page `lang`, so you can translate between any pair of supported languages.
+- The chosen language is saved in `localStorage` and applied again on later page loads. If the language model still has to be downloaded, the reader is asked to click **Translate**, because downloads require a user gesture.
+- Core logic: `src/utils/translation.ts`. UI: `src/components/TranslateControl.tsx`.
